      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5.1 Folk Dances"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Bastar Dussehra is celebrated for 75 days, making it the longest tribal festival without idol immersion.",
        "Pandavani is Chhattisgarh's renowned musical narration of the Mahabharata, divided into Vedamati and Kapalik styles.",
        "Bhoramdeo Temple in Kabirdham, built by the Phani Nagvanshi dynasty, is known as the Khajuraho of Chhattisgarh.",
        "Dhokra metal craft utilizes the ancient lost-wax casting technique (Cire Perdue) predominantly practiced in the Bastar region.",
        "Hareli is observed as the first agricultural festival of Chhattisgarh, dedicated to worshipping farming tools and cattle."
      ],
      "id": "765xq4l"
    },
